=== TITLE: USG Upper Abdomen (Hepatobiliary & Renal) ===
=== IMPRESSION ===
NO SIGNIFICANT ABNORMALITY DETECTED IN UPPER ABDOMINAL ORGANS.

=== FINDINGS ===
STUDY: ULTRASONOGRAPHY OF UPPER ABDOMEN

FINDINGS:
- LIVER: Normal in size (13.5 cm) and outline. Uniform parenchymal echotexture without focal mass lesion. No intrahepatic biliary dilatation.
- GALL BLADDER: Well-distended with thin, smooth walls. Lumen clear without calculus. CBD normal in caliber.
- PANCREAS: Head, body, and tail are normal in size and echogenicity. MPD is not dilated.
- SPLEEN: Normal in size (9.5 cm) and homogeneous.
- KIDNEYS: Bilateral kidneys are normal in size, shape, and cortical thickness. No calculus or hydronephrosis.